  ('af455a4d-f54b-4634-85b6-ad1a9b1e5d4f', '30879f74-10a5-4fca-802e-083ce664f5fd', 'Makoto Misumi', '深澄真', '', 'https://s4.anilist.co/file/anilistcdn/character/large/b138137-yBtJdBlRziS9.png', 'main', 'Makoto Misumi is the Main Protagonist of this series. He is a one of the three World Traveler''s who got sent to the [Goddess](https://anilist.co/character/221535/Megami)'' World.

Originally meant to be the only person to be sent to the other world as per the contract between his parents and the Goddess, but because of her own preferences in beauty standards, she abandons and throws Makoto to the edge of her world into the Wasteland, while secretly kidnapping two other people from Earth and sending them to her world as Heroes. [Tsukuyomi](https://anilist.co/character/195917/Tsukuyomi), the Moon God of Earth who worked as the middleman for the completion of the contract, helped Makoto and provided him with his blessing and told him to be free and live as he wants to.

~!In the Goddess'' World, he is also known by the alias "Raidou Kuzunoha" (in WN/LN) or "Makoto Kuzunoha" (in Manga), a powerful merchant and skilled teacher.!~

', 'Dallas Reid', '花江夏樹', '2026-05-28T05:38:31.162719+00:00', '2026-05-28T16:06:42.596237+00:00'),
  ('aa45da21-6304-460d-932b-e6214da329fd', '0235fd16-36de-4dcf-99a6-1123a10ce2ab', 'Coco', 'ココ', '', 'https://s4.anilist.co/file/anilistcdn/character/large/b129840-B2CVE0TIcKpT.png', 'main', 'She is a young girl who becomes an apprentice witch under the witch Qifrey after her initial accidental use of forbidden magic turned her mother to crystal. She hopes to search the Tower of Books for the book containing the magic, in order to reverse its effects on her mother.

She is quite a dork for magic, with a child-like (even for her age) widen eyed look whenever she sees things that are common for every other witch. The very magic that inspired her was simple magic made by Qifrey''s watcher that caused glowstone path to light up.', 'Anjali Kunapaneni', '本村玲奈', '2026-05-17T19:16:48.777476+00:00', '2026-05-17T19:17:10.917383+00:00'),
  ('48bb308e-3f75-47b3-84dc-61ab384e2976', 'f967f9fe-5927-4e52-91de-e461f04d5665', 'Ruby Hoshino', '星野ルビー', '', 'https://s4.anilist.co/file/anilistcdn/character/large/b183884-iyo3BmTuhJ0l.jpg', 'main', '__Height:__ 158 cm (5''2")

[Ai Hoshino](https://anilist.co/character/172759/Ai-Hoshino)''s daughter, and the younger twin sister of [Aquamarine Hoshino](https://anilist.co/character/183885). 
~!She was previously a patient named Sarina under Goro''s care. Due to her illness, she was wheelchair-bound. After discovering B-Komachi, she had always aspired to be an idol although her condition kept her from achieving her dream. Since being reincarnated as Ruby, she is now working towards her dream of being an idol like Ai. To do so she''s currently working with Strawberry Productions to revive B-Komachi along with Arima Kana and Memcho.!~', 'Yurie Igoma', '伊駒ゆりえ', '2026-03-08T10:29:58.01664+00:00', '2026-03-08T10:35:47.896393+00:00'),
  ('7139778e-9283-4cab-bb94-f504d7ff69d2', 'c9325986-caa8-42ca-9d68-b7e50f073ef0', 'Sakura Himedaka', '姫鷹さくら', '春の護衛官', 'https://s4.anilist.co/file/anilistcdn/character/large/b319956-TRREaamL2ulm.png', 'main', '__Occupation:__ Guard of Spring

A young woman who cherishes [Hinagiku](https://anilist.co/character/319954/Hinagiku-Kayo) greatly as her best friend and retainer. She falls into despair after Hinagiku''s kidnapping and cuts ties with the Agent of Winter, [Rosei](https://anilist.co/character/319955/Rosei-Kantsubaki), and his Guard, [Itecho](https://anilist.co/character/319957/Itechou-Kangetsu), soon afterwards, despite her lingering feelings for Itecho.

~!After Hinagiku''s return, Sakura gradually lets the Winter duo back into her and Hinagiku''s lives once the four reunite, internally accepting her feelings for Itecho and becoming closer to him in the process.!~', 'Marisa Duran', '青山吉能', '2026-05-26T03:44:01.839886+00:00', '2026-05-26T06:33:08.283742+00:00'),
  ('6ba9d01d-d2a2-40f4-a83b-bbd08f4e4027', 'e2dfcb41-d205-451b-93fe-3a101eafeae3', 'Armin Arlert', 'アルミン・アルレルト', 'Armin Arlelt', 'https://s4.anilist.co/file/anilistcdn/character/large/b46494-g7xYYuBtYPnO.png', 'main', '__Height:__ 163 cm (5''4")
__Position:__ 104th Trainees Squad, Survey Corps
__Relatives:__ [Grandfather](https://anilist.co/character/84313/Armin-no-Ojiisan)

Armin is a young boy who was born and raised in the Shiganshina District within the walls, being childhood friends with both [Eren Yeager](https://anilist.co/character/40882/Eren-Yeager) and [Mikasa Ackerman](https://anilist.co/character/40881). After Wall Maria was breached, he chose to join Mikasa and Eren in joining the military, both to try to make a good and meaningful impact on the world, and to fulfill his dream of seeing the outside world.

Even when he was young, the naturally curious Armin has always had a deep fascination with the world beyond the Walls. As a child, he found and studied an illegal book about the outside world that was owned by his grandfather. He often shared the book and information contained in it with Eren Yeager, his best friend, and his dreams of seeing the world outside the walls. Armin was branded a heretic by other children for his unusual interest in the outside world and was thus frequently picked on. Too timid to defend himself, Armin would often rely on his friends Eren and Mikasa Ackerman to protect him from local bullies. This, coupled with his frail physique, was a deep shame for Armin, leading him to have poor self-esteem and to believe that he is a burden to others. Because of this, Armin has always been very eager to prove his worth, especially towards his close friends. 

Armin is known to be exceptionally loyal and selfless. He constantly worries for the safety of his friends, and he is always prepared to throw himself into dangerous situations to save them. Alongside his kindhearted nature and emotionally intelligence, Armin is a very analytical person. He likes to think deeply about situations and solve problems using his mind. These personality traits, in conjunction with his intelligence, good judgment, level headedness, ability to plan ahead, come up with creative ideas and to think outside the box, are what make him a great tactician. Although he may appear among the physically weakest of the 104th Training Corps, his incredible intelligence and strategic genius makes him an invaluable asset to any team.
', 'Jessie James Grelle', '井上麻里奈', '2026-03-08T10:30:08.408085+00:00', '2026-03-08T10:35:58.620351+00:00'),
  ('3169f521-4976-4fa4-bbec-7fb32173c02c', 'd4bc6bb1-8eb4-4c05-a055-303148a573c3', 'Tsuyoshi  Mukouda', '向田剛志', 'ムコーダ, Mukohda', 'https://s4.anilist.co/file/anilistcdn/character/large/b157881-uLcY9D0sFskw.png', 'main', 'A salaryman summoned from modern Japan. He possesses the unique skill, "Online Supermarket", which allows him to buy goods from modern Japan any time, any place. The food he buys with his skill has buffing effects, making anyone who eats it become much stronger than before. He is very good at cooking, but is a coward by nature.

Mukouda was first seen wearing a suit and tie, a huge difference from his co-summoned heroes which were wearing school uniforms. After selling his former clothes, he now wears a dark green shirt with long sleeves that he usually kept folded when he cooks.', 'Aaron Campbell', '内田雄馬', '2025-11-01T07:27:23.614626+00:00', '2026-03-08T10:36:04.435331+00:00'),
